; JSON round-trip property fixtures.
;
; Each top-level form below is parsed, encoded with `Json.toJson(canonical)`,
; decoded with `Json.fromJson(canonical)`, then canonical-printed; the
; result must equal the canonical print of the original. Forms here exist
; to pin specific encoding paths against regressions.

; Atoms — non-keyword scalars at top level are safe; bare top-level
; keywords are not, because the parser greedy-pairs `:kw value` and
; would expand top-level keyword pairs into degenerate split-roots.
; Keyword atom encoding is exercised by the dedicated tests above.
nil
true
false
42
3.5
"hello"

; Vectors with mixed element kinds. (Vectors hold only positional values;
; bare keyword tokens like `:a` parse as positional keyword "flags". A
; `:kw v` pair inside a vector is promoted to two positional elements,
; preserving source order.)
[1 2 3]
[:a :b :c]
[1 "bar" true nil 3.5]
[1 :foo "bar" true nil]

; Forms with keyword pairs and positional children.
(scene :bpm 130 (canvas :name "main" [1 2 3]))
(masagin/verb :ops 1 :gain 0.5)

; Symbol values inside a safe-expression form (binds inside `let`).
(let [r 0.5] (vec3 r r r))

; Reserved-prefix head: head literally `$form`. Sigil escape must keep
; this from colliding with the discriminator slot.
($form a b)

; Reserved-prefix keyword keys: `:$form` and `:$kw` as user data.
(thing :$form "x" :$kw "y" "tail")

; Unit-suffixed numbers — round-trip via {"$num": [value, "unit"]}.
90deg
0.5em
-50%
[4b 90deg 50% 250ms]
(thing :angle 90deg :delay 250ms :scale 0.5em)
(deep -50% 1.5e2hz)
